[22.83,"o","# Mission: Fix hello world greeting (parallix-adhoc-0001)\r\n\r\n## Goal\r\nMake the existing hello-world entry point emit exactly `Hello, World!`.\r\n\r\n## Why Now\r\nThe repository's visible starter greeting is incorrect; correcting this isolated output restores the \b expected first-run behavior without expanding the sample application.\r\n\r\n## Refinement Signals\r\n- Predicted NEL bucket: Small (0–80)\r\n- Confidence: High\r\n- Selection note: activate as-is\r\n- Main drivers: one existing greeting value and its direct regression coverage\r\n\r\n## Scope\r\n- Locate the existing hello-world entry point and change only its greeting value.\r\n- Add or update direct automated coverage that invokes that entry point and checks the exact greetin \bg text.\r\n- Run the repository verification command in Gates.\r\n\r\n## Out of Scope\r\n- Changing command-line arguments, program flow, packaging, dependencies, or project configuration.\r\n\u001b[7mmissions/parallix-adhoc-0001/MISSION.md\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
